SECTION_5_AUDIENCE_INTELLIGENCE
who_they_are: Women (predominantly 18-40) actively searching in late July/August for manicure inspiration specific to this exact month — not summer in general. Many are transitioning from vacation mode back to routine (work, school pickup, back-to-school prep) and want their nails to reflect that shift without fully abandoning summer color energy. Search happens heavily on Pinterest and mobile, often the night before or day of a salon appointment or DIY session.

what_they_want_from_this_post: A single, visually rich reference that shows them what's actually current for August specifically (not generic "summer nails" from June) — colors, shapes, and finishes they can screenshot and bring to a nail tech, or replicate at home.

what_frustrates_them: Existing content is often outdated (posted in June, reused for August), overly product-focused (shopping links over inspiration), or narrowly focused on one angle only (just colors, or just one influencer's set) rather than a full range of ideas across styles and skin tones.

top_5_pain_points:
1. Confusion over whether to keep bright summer colors or start transitioning toward fall tones in August specifically
2. Difficulty finding designs that work for both "still on vacation" and "back to routine/school" contexts
3. Uncertainty about which shapes and lengths photograph and wear best in late-summer heat and humidity
4. Wanting something Pinterest-worthy but achievable without a $100+ salon visit
5. Overwhelm from too many generic "summer nail" roundups that don't feel tailored to the August moment (birthday season, back-to-school, last vacations)

